# Template for /etc/homelab-watchdog/env on the Proxmox host (10.0.0.2),
# mode 0600, never committed with real values. Read by
# deploy/homelab-watchdog.sh (via `source`, not systemd's EnvironmentFile=,
# so the same file works whether the script is run by
# deploy/homelab-watchdog.timer or by hand).
#
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN is a copy of the same token already in the agent's own
# /etc/homelab-agent/env on LXC 104 - copy it once here, and again if it's
# ever rotated. A host-local copy, not a live `pct exec` read on every run,
# is the deliberate choice for this file specifically: the one case this
# watchdog exists to catch that homelab-agent.service's own `OnFailure=`
# alert cannot (see deploy/homelab-agent-alert@.service) is the container
# itself being down - and a token source that also needs the container up
# would fail to notify in exactly that case. See docs/deploy.md for the
# one-time setup.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# Where the watchdog posts. Defaults to #homelab-alerts (same default as
# the agent's own SLACK_CHANNEL_STATUS) if left unset.
# SLACK_CHANNEL=#homelab-alerts
